 "etapas": [
  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Reflexive verbs",
     "texto": [
      "Unlike English («I get up»), many everyday verbs take a pronoun in front, as in Spanish: **je me lève** (I get up), **je me douche** (I shower), **je me couche** (I go to bed).",
      "Before a vowel, **me** loses its e: **je m'habille** (I get dressed), **je m'appelle**.",
      "In a negative sentence, **ne** goes before the reflexive pronoun and **pas** after the verb: **Je ne me couche pas tard** (I don't go to bed late)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "tabla",
     "titulo": "The verb «se lever» (to get up)",
