    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Parts of the day",
     "texto": [
      "**Le matin** (in the morning), **l'après-midi** (in the afternoon), **le soir** (in the evening, depending on the time), **la nuit** (at night). To say when something happens, they are normally used without a preposition, unlike English.",
      "Meals: **le petit déjeuner** (breakfast), **le déjeuner** (lunch), **le dîner** (dinner). And their verbs: **déjeuner** (to have lunch) and **dîner** (to have dinner).",
      "**Tous les jours** = every day. **Tôt** = early. **Tard** = late."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    }
   ]
